who went on to work with animals after a  career on the disney channel does the  kid from erie indiana have an  appropriately weird job now that he's an  adult not all former child stars burn  out some of them just quietly move on to  other professions in stanley kubrick's  classic 1980 adaptation of stephen  king's the shining the role of the  troubled psychically gifted danny  torrance was played by newcomer danny  lloyd  lloyd discussed his time making the  horror film in a 2017 interview with the  guardian as he revealed that he enjoyed  the experience and has fond memories of  it but he hasn't kept up an acting  career in the decades since his reasons  for leaving the industry have nothing to  do with the film itself instead the work  just dried up for him lloyd continued to  audition a process that can be grueling  but he didn't mind it too much as he  told the guardian i always enjoyed it it  was exciting but as i got a little bit  older it got kind of boring then i had  to tell my parents that i was ready to  quit which they were fine with they were  never stage parents they made sure i had  a normal upbringing these days lloyd is  a biology professor at a community  college in kentucky and he's happy with  the showbiz legacy according to him i  don't regret trying acting when i  decided to stop i don't regret that  either  if you know mara wilson you most likely  recognize her from early 90s family  classics like mrs doubtfire miracle on  34th street and of course as the title  character in matilda she was one of  those child stars who seemed to be wise  beyond her years at no point did it ever  appear like she was mugging for the  camera or attempting too hard to be a  cute kid instead there was a natural  quality in her performances that was  absolutely unique to her and that may  very well be why her work in those films  is still fondly remembered all these  years later while talking to npr in 2016  wilson explained that her departure from  acting happened gradually almost without  her even realizing it after her mother's  passing acting became the only constant  in her life but she didn't have the same  enthusiasm for it as puberty struck she  was embarrassed by the natural processes  of growing up and it was difficult to go  through publicly eventually she found  that she could survive without acting so  she instead focused on writing she  composed a play called sheeple in 2013  and her memoir where am i now was  released in 2016. where is she now where  did she disappear to  k panabeker began her career in 2001 in  a short film called temptation and she  also recorded some voices in the  animated pixar classic monsters inc her  star then rose so quickly that she  worked almost non-stop for the next 10  years she showed up on tv shows like  angel and law order special victims unit  while also co-starring in the disney  channel series phil of the future  additionally she appeared in tv movies  like read it and weep alongside her  older sister danielle and one of the  biggest titles on her resume is the 2009  remake of fame despite her continued  success panabaker ultimately decided to  walk away from acting she revealed to  her fans on twitter her very simple  reason for leaving the entertainment  industry behind while also sharing some  life advice as she wrote i just lost the  love for acting life is short we spend  too much time at work gotta do what you  love and i love my job that job that she  loves so much is working with animals as  she now has a gig as a zookeeper at  disney world's animal kingdom  it would be hard to imagine anyone  living on planet earth for the past few  decades who hasn't heard of the olsen  twins the pair absolutely dominated  family entertainment during the early  1990s they got their start playing  youngest sister michelle tanner on the  iconic family sitcom full house and they  then shot into the pop culture  stratosphere thanks to their numerous tv  movies like to grandmother's house we go  and double double toil and trouble as  well as a mountain of direct video  movies and other official merchandise in  2006 the olsen twins launched the row a  luxury fashion line that they've worked  on perfecting for over 15 years in a  rare interview they sat down with id  magazine in 2021 to celebrate the  success of their venture the  conversation included very little  discussion of their acting careers  though they did mention that the reason  they're not open with the public about  their lives is they've always been  discreet people as that's how they were  raised while we may not know their exact  reasons for entering the fashion world  and leaving entertainment behind it  seems pretty clear that they're happy  with their current careers  lyanna creel's biggest claim to fame is  probably the 10 episodes of saved by the  bell she appeared in during the show's  final season in which she was set up as  a foil for zack morris she played the  headstrong torrey scott who wouldn't  fall easily for his charm before that  her first credit was in another beloved  series a 1987 episode of the abc sitcom  growing pains shortly afterwards she and  her sisters starred in the tv movies  parent trap 3 and parent trap hawaiian  honeymoon alongside acting legend haley  mills who starred in the original parent  trap movie as well as good morning miss  bliss a series that became saved by the  bell creole may not be acting anymore  but she's still involved with producing  visual content through creel studio a  production company that she runs with  her wife it's the company's commitment  to philanthropy that really helps it  stand out according to its website we  believe the good life is about more than  just material comforts it's also about  living a life marked by doing good in  illuminating all aspects of the good  life we convey an enlightened sense of  luxury lifestyle content creole also  started an app that assists real estate  professionals in creating content  originally a dancer amy foster is  probably best remembered for two  projects the 1989 shelley long comedy  troop beverly hills which was about a  troop of rich privileged girl scouts and  the nbc sitcom punky brewster on which  she played the rich entitled and  slightly oblivious margot but those are  only two credits on a long and  impressive resume that foster assembled  over the course of an 11 year acting  career while catching up with her punky  co-star cherry johnson on the cherries  world podcast in 2021 foster discussed  what she's been up to since walking away  from acting for a brief time she entered  the music industry and moved to  nashville however she wanted to be with  her family in los angeles and her  husband got a job there working as a  firefighter after the birth of her  daughter she decided that she would  rather be home instead of working in  showbiz so she might have the most  grown-up gig of anybody on this list  michael oliver's career may have only  lasted six years but when your first  role out of the gate is the meanest  little kid in cinema there isn't much  else you need to do after that he also  had small roles in other notable movies  like forrest gump and a racer but it's  his portrayal of junior and problem  child and problem child 2 that left the  biggest impact in 2015 oliver was a  guest on his problem child co-star  gilbert gottfried's amazing colossal  podcast the two reminisced about working  on the original film learning from the  late john ritter and what happened to  oliver in the years since around the  time that oliver's parents pursued legal  action against the studio for failing to  pay them the money they were owed they  lost their house and he was losing  interest in acting he likened his life  experience to the opposite of a kid  wondering what it must be like to be  famous to him he was looking at the  lives of normal kids and wondering what  that was like at the time of the  interview he was working in the tech  support industry  the biggest title on omri katz's resume  is probably the prime time soap opera  dallas on which he played john ross  ewing iii but anyone who grew up in the  early 90s will surely know him best for  the quirky tv show eerie indiana and the  halloween classic hocus pocus he also  worked with director joe dante in the  1993 movie matinee a cult classic ode to  60s b-movie schlock and cold war  tensions in march 2020 katz posted a  message on his instagram that he was  getting into the cannabis apparel  business as he wrote being a member of  the cannabis community for almost 20  years now and jumping through hoops of  fire to get here i'm proud to announce  our online apparel store will be opening  up soon the store in question is called  the married dangsters and the about  section on the website declares we the  merry dangsters are ambassadors of the  cannabis culture with deep roots within  the traditional cannabis community we  represent positivity herb and unity  ariana richards appeared in a few films  and tv shows in the 90s that are still a  big deal today she surely best  remembered his lex in the original  jurassic park additionally she also  appeared alongside kevin bacon in 1990s  tremors she played the title character's  love interest in 1995's angus and she  turned in a heartbreaking performance as  a young girl being abused by her father  in an episode of boy meets world in 2020  richards spoke with amblin entertainment  about her experience making jurassic  park and what her life's like now a  painter from an early age she took part  in a mentorship through the california  arts club after college she credits  everything she learned during those four  years with sending her down her current  path as a professional painter  eva amore started her acting career in  the 1992 film bob roberts alongside the  father of her half siblings tim robbins  her mother is actress susan sarandon and  the two work together in dead man  walking earthly possessions anywhere but  here and the banger sisters amore also  appeared on huge tv shows like friends  and how i met your mother her acting  career was still going strong for  several years until she ultimately  decided to step away in 2016. following  the birth of her daughter amore realized  that she couldn't raise a child to spend  her life doing something that made her  happy when she wasn't doing that herself  while talking with yahoo finance in 2019  she explained that she made a list of  things that did make her happy her  then-husband told her it looked like a  lifestyle blog and he encouraged her to  learn how to make a living in an online  space her blog happily eva after then  launched in 2015 and it covers her  favorite topics which are style decor  food and crafting  even if you've never seen a single film  starring this tiny mega star chances are  you still recognize the name simply put  there would be no olsen twins empire  without shirley temple her image was so  recognizable and popular that it was  plastered all over various kinds of  merchandise in the 1930s she was such a  huge star so early in life but then she  retired from acting at the tender age of  22 considering that she started her life  on screen at the age of three and  starred in 34 films over a 14-year  period it's safe to say that she had a  full career before most people even got  started  during the late 50s and into the early  60s temple briefly returned to  entertainment both in front of and  behind the camera she then transitioned  to a new role in 1969 when she became a  diplomat as she traveled around the  world she witnessed atrocities that put  her on track to becoming the ambassador  to ghana in 1974  and then in 1989 she was appointed by  president george h.w bush to be the  first female ambassador to  czechoslovakia check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite actors  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel 